1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,418
New drug to regenerate lost teeth.

2
00:00:03,212 --> 00:00:04,324
Multiplying teeth.

3
00:00:05,122 --> 00:00:06,164
Regrowing teeth.

4
00:00:06,962 --> 00:00:08,756
Headlines like these travel fast.

5
00:00:09,555 --> 00:00:10,886
The follow-up rarely does.

6
00:00:11,685 --> 00:00:12,854
So, years later:

7
00:00:13,027 --> 00:00:13,780
what came of it?

8
00:00:14,430 --> 00:00:16,270
“What came of it?” is a public record of what

9
00:00:16,281 --> 00:00:18,226
followed reported medical breakthroughs.

10
00:00:19,021 --> 00:00:20,514
Each claim gets one page:

11
00:00:20,722 --> 00:00:22,505
one treatment, for one condition.

12
00:00:23,303 --> 00:00:25,086
At the top is where it stands now.

13
00:00:25,884 --> 00:00:28,326
This one, first reported in 2021,

14
00:00:28,558 --> 00:00:30,039
has reached a Phase 1 trial:

15
00:00:30,178 --> 00:00:31,451
an early trial in people,

16
00:00:31,625 --> 00:00:32,400
checking safety.

17
00:00:33,050 --> 00:00:35,365
Underneath are the dated records that say so.

18
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:38,637
A trial registered in October 2024.

19
00:00:39,436 --> 00:00:41,033
The same trial shown as complete

20
00:00:41,044 --> 00:00:42,653
in October 2025.

21
00:00:43,452 --> 00:00:44,517
Every record links to the

22
00:00:44,528 --> 00:00:45,547
registry that holds it,

23
00:00:45,732 --> 00:00:47,005
so you can check it yourself.

24
00:00:47,804 --> 00:00:48,903
And what was promised sits

25
00:00:48,915 --> 00:00:50,281
beside what was recorded.

26
00:00:50,931 --> 00:00:52,806
The status is set by fixed rules,

27
00:00:52,991 --> 00:00:54,623
from public registry records.

28
00:00:55,418 --> 00:00:56,610
No editor decides it,

29
00:00:56,795 --> 00:00:58,438
and no AI model does either.

30
00:00:59,237 --> 00:01:01,297
When nothing new has been recorded for years,

31
00:01:01,471 --> 00:01:02,744
the page says exactly that:

32
00:01:02,929 --> 00:01:04,434
no signal for ten years.

33
00:01:05,232 --> 00:01:06,656
That describes the records.

34
00:01:07,455 --> 00:01:09,191
It is not a verdict on the treatment.

35
00:01:09,841 --> 00:01:11,230
Seen a headline shared again?

36
00:01:12,025 --> 00:01:13,321
Paste the article's link into

37
00:01:13,332 --> 00:01:14,698
the box on the home page.

38
00:01:15,497 --> 00:01:16,538
If the claim is tracked,

39
00:01:16,631 --> 00:01:18,159
the answer comes back at once.

40
00:01:18,957 --> 00:01:20,902
The link is compared inside your browser,

41
00:01:21,075 --> 00:01:21,851
and sent nowhere.

42
00:01:22,501 --> 00:01:24,191
There is also a browser extension,

43
00:01:24,330 --> 00:01:25,475
for Chrome and Safari.

44
00:01:26,270 --> 00:01:27,335
Open it on an article,

45
00:01:27,578 --> 00:01:28,817
and it shows the tracked claim's

46
00:01:28,828 --> 00:01:29,754
status right there.

47
00:01:30,553 --> 00:01:31,919
If the article is not tracked,

48
00:01:32,138 --> 00:01:34,175
it can search the trial registries live.

49
00:01:34,974 --> 00:01:36,629
Those results are marked automatic

50
00:01:36,641 --> 00:01:37,196
and unreviewed,

51
00:01:37,405 --> 00:01:39,419
and every match shows its confidence score.

52
00:01:40,069 --> 00:01:41,261
No medical advice.

53
00:01:42,056 --> 00:01:43,039
No verdicts.

54
00:01:43,838 --> 00:01:45,134
Only what the records show,

55
00:01:45,389 --> 00:01:45,887
and when.

56
00:01:46,685 --> 00:01:47,484
What came of it?

57
00:01:48,282 --> 00:01:50,366
Find out, at whatcameofit.com.

